Crumb licensing
===============

Code
----

Unless a file states otherwise, all source code, scripts, configuration, and
documentation in this repository are licensed under the MIT License. The
canonical license text is in `LICENSES/preferred/MIT`.

    SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

Visual assets
-------------

Visual and brand assets under `crumb.elixpo/public/`, including icons, mascot
art, and social artwork, are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International. The canonical license text is in
`LICENSES/preferred/CC-BY-4.0`.

    SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0

Trademarks
----------

Copyright licences grant rights in the files. They do not grant trademark
rights or permission to imply endorsement. The Elixpo and Oreo names, mascot,
E-badge, domains, and related source identifiers are governed separately by
`TRADEMARKS.md`. That policy does not limit the MIT or CC-BY-4.0 permissions
in the files themselves.

Third-party material
--------------------

Third-party components retain their respective licences. See
`LICENSES/notices/notice-board` and the corresponding dependency metadata.

Contributions
-------------

Contributions are accepted under the licence applying to the contributed
area: MIT for code and documentation, or CC-BY-4.0 for visual assets. The
Developer Certificate of Origin applies to every commit. No contributor
licence agreement is required.

